{"title":"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution II</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all real numbers a for which there exists non-negative reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/1/971c9466ae2b8b57a5dda45ad33d49072de0c365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{1}, \\ldots, x_{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"11\" /> which satisfy the relations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa0fc4c3b5c39b5fe2220a85286d16b9d1a5ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{5} kx_{k}=a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/3181d6fbfa782d488ffe6fdd63a4a858e78cbb84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{5} k^{3}x_{k}=a^{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"110\" height=\"50\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c47703780142416f928a28314cd8a37760b97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{5} k^{5}x_{k}=a^{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"109\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fde823bb0842c450164627a53ba7166031d6885.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma_1= \\sum_{k=1}^{5} kx_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"104\" height=\"56\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5af6350f66335487b7b4a47633dd9817039ae181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma_2=\\sum_{k=1}^{5} k^{3}x_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"111\" height=\"56\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/5671e38a0250188a11a5952e478c7d4245fefc34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma_3=\\sum_{k=1}^{5} k^{5}x_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"111\" height=\"56\" />. For all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74b1cbbdaca0e408ddc58f6fc51912d856b2e56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j\\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />, let<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b56a4eccc2eeebaab5f870cda8312eddc8c9e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(i,j)=i^2j^2\\Sigma_1-(i^2+j^2)\\Sigma_2+\\Sigma_3\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"20\" />Then we have on one hand<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e0d22d3e1a971f0ca9d134bec7282c0ab01461.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(i,j)=i^2j^2\\Sigma_1-(i^2+j^2)\\Sigma_2+\\Sigma_3=\\sum_{k=1}^5(i^2j^2k-(i^2+j^2)k^3+k^5)x_k =\\sum_{k=1}^5k(i^2j^2-(i^2+j^2)k^2+k^4)x_k\\]\" width=\"740\" height=\"51\" />Therefore \\\\(1)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d30f9c854cbff4ea35e5e05b329d5da6450cf50a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(i,j)=\\sum_{k=1}^5k(k^2-i^2)(k^2-j^2)x_k\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"51\" />and on the other hand \\\\ (2)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/7056e9ff66736d1c2d08200727670dd79d8ed8ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(i,j)=i^2j^2a-(i^2+j^2)a^2+a^3=a(a-i^2)(a-j^2)\\]\" width=\"411\" height=\"20\" />Then from (1) we have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac0d33f30e130fbbe7c0f346e92a952fdef463e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(0,5)=\\sum_{k=1}^5k^3(k^2-5^2)x_k\\leq 0\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"51\" />and from (2)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e47de2de2c4422884d3dd67202f3ce17d3f5d9eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(0,5)=a^2(a-25)\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df120a38729f1e1a0913d49ba4609220ff16aa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in [0,25]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> Besides we also have from (1)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c4462a0e1dbdc5946100caf8d44526ba3d0188b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(0,1)=\\sum_{k=1}^5k^3(k^2-1)x_k\\geq 0\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"51\" />and from (2)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6db4f0c65a9a9eb2ed42ebef776dd68a73502b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(0,1)=a^2(a-1)\\geq 0 \\implies a\\notin (0,1)\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"20\" />and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea256dfe34c6eedd4d1e350fb397cd824dddc15d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1,2,3,4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b96fc5ecf2ea245299be24c945515ede639102.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(n,n+1)=\\sum_{k=1}^5k(k^2-n^2)(k^2-(n+1)^2)x_k\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"51\" />where in the right hand we have that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e6164c02f0f443125e99f53b91d3d96f3c882d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k&lt;n \\implies (k^2-n^2)&lt;0, (k^2-(n+1)^2)&lt;0\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"20\" />, so<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/485d1cfe551264c3bd2f823d81ed6ebb7d7943c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(k^2-n^2)(k^2-(n+1)^2)&gt;0\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"20\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08dc916f8fcc405c4fb4f04a6384d0914bc8b196.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k=n,n+1 , \\implies (k^2-n^2)(k^2-(n+1)^2)=0\\]\" width=\"370\" height=\"20\" />and<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffbf63b5acef55ab2b800c872904245a14e4711.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k&gt;n \\implies (k^2-n^2)(k^2-(n+1)^2)&gt;0\\]\" width=\"317\" height=\"20\" />, so<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f826909cdbd3344404e3ea7dcd9c04496553dad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(n,n+1)\\geq 0\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea256dfe34c6eedd4d1e350fb397cd824dddc15d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1,2,3,4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> From the latter and (2) we also have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b027896330b83e9a9c3ed80c181c76cb867e0b61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma(n,n+1)=a(a-n^2)(a-(n+1)^2))\\geq 0\\implies a\\notin (n^2,(n+1)^2)\\]\" width=\"479\" height=\"20\" />So we have that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28fed36f7937afc9686aefc9a7083e2d94f4203a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\in [0,25]-\\bigcup_{n=0}^4(n^2,(n+1^2))=\\{0,1,4,9,16,25\\}\\]\" width=\"383\" height=\"50\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e779efc0abff653a40a092b2acb431c5de95d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111f9ccae134f1425b67f3797d359203fc735833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,3,4,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" /> take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/a/09aebe9c31ba1b39f5cca78ff8b8844ca6e0122e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed9e5e2e7b23553218a50466b17d168756a70ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_j=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c837afd0c6c2ad88d095c6a6c3b9b949897e31d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j\\neq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/4494e4df6fe4113ce73428be8d519e8d5de45390.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma_1=k^2=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e67d5322cfbf72802c1972b99179ab45e0f178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma_2=k^3k=k^4=a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/d/87d10b0d6dad5231b6a7d1bac322c311a248b8dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma_3=k^5k=k^6=a^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_II\">Solution II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Applying Cauchy-Schwarz on the three equations yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a81b79be3d71c7ba16d3e5689f96555976c0e09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot a^3 = \\left(\\sum_{k=1}^5 kx_k\\right)\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^5 k^5x_k\\right)\\geq \\left(\\sum_{k=1}^5 k^3x_k\\right)^2=(a^2)^2\\]\" width=\"431\" height=\"57\" />\nSo this implies the following vectors are multiples of each other:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e406f680820a55cf46a2f28c89692908ab6d1178.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_1,2x_2,3x_3,4x_4,5x_5) =\\lambda (x_1,2^5x_2,3^5x_3,4^5x_4,5^5x_5)\\quad \\quad \\lambda\\in \\mathbb{R}^+\\]\" width=\"496\" height=\"20\" />\nThis is only possible when at most one of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />'s are nonzero. Hence cycling through the cases where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcbf2fb1eb9dc273030f63bc3fab6d34620a047b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, we get the choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e78bf9b8413c5cdc0da8e4e7b4472069e845a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1,4,9,16,25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" /> and the case of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO\" title=\"1979 IMO\">1979 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1979 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173118\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 227/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8049/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.086      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.086      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20530:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173118 and revision id 271812. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}